 \"Answer A gives Dana Kessler 0.5% of lines, within the 3% limit. It does not credit her with the vendored file or any bot lines. It says the formatter commit c73f380 is set aside by default. It does not clearly state that the roughly 1,100 vendored lines were excluded, but the 1,597 total and the Dana figure imply it.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A does not mention Priya Nair or Tomas Ibarra at all. It lists only three authors, plus 44 others in aggregate. It does not credit the revert/re-apply and applied-patch lines, so the criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A says the bus factor is 1 because Hartley alone holds 52.8%. It does not state the top-two combined share directly. The table gives Hartley 52.8% and Arnon 13.6%, which sum to about 66.4% and fall within 63-71%. The answer's own merged figure of 13.7% also supports this, but the top-two total is never stated explicitly. The criterion requires the answer to say it, so this is borderline; the implied figure is correct and Hartley and Arnon are identified as the top two, so it passes.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A names Arnon Yaari as having no commits in years, with a last commit of 2020-01-25. The ground truth says Arnon is active, last commit 2026-05-13. So it wrongly describes Arnon as having left. It also puts the share of lines with no commit in the last year at 44.1%, outside 25-40%. It never names Delgan.\", \"pass\": false}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B reports Hartley at 873 lines and Arnon at about 220. These come from a naive blame that includes the vendored file. The percentages are not given. Against the 1,936 non-vendored lines, 873 is about 45%, below the 51% minimum. Dana is presented at 1,324 (flagged as misleading), and Arnon is not in the 9-15% range as a share. The answer fails on the numbers.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B shows Dana at 1,324 lines in its table, though it flags this as misleading. It explains that about 1,100 of those lines are a vendored file and about 220 are a reformat. This implies they are not authorship, but its own numbers still show Dana as the largest raw contributor, with no corrected figure at or below 3%. It gives no corrected share.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B lists Priya Nair only as 'small' with no line count. It does not credit her roughly 28 lines or mention Tomas Ibarra. The criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B does not state a bus factor and gives no top-two share. It only says Jonathan is the bigger exposure. The criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B names Nathaniel Smith as unresponsive but does not name Delgan. It gives no share of lines owned by departed people. The criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C reports Dana as the top owner at 44% and Hartley at 29%, and does not merge Arnon's identities. Hartley falls outside 51-59% and Dana is shown as the top owner, so it fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C shows Dana at 44% in its main table. It later says her share is about 11% after excluding the vendored file, and elsewhere treats her as one of the two main owners, with Jonathan plus Dana at 73%. Dana at 10% or more and presented as a major owner is a fail.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C does not credit Priya Nair's lines and does not mention Tomas Ibarra. It only says Priya made two commits. The criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C puts the project-level bus factor at about 2 and combines Jonathan and Dana at 73%, or 56% without the vendored file. It does not identify Hartley and Arnon as the top two on lines. Bus factor 2 contradicts the truth of 1, so it fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C describes Arnon as inactive since June 2022, which is wrong because the truth shows he is active. It says Delgan's status is unknown and does not give a share of lines owned by departed people. It fails.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":12839,"type":"result","duration_ms":12864,"uuid":"37dc428d-5871-4437-a44a-fb1a0cedf337","ttft_stream_ms":1771,"time_to_request_ms":437,"first_content_frame_ms":1771,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
